fix: AI calendars/timelines render as diagrams, not raw code

The tutor was correctly producing a Gantt study calendar, but fenced it as
```gantt (the diagram type) rather than ```mermaid, and omitted the leading
type keyword — so both renderers fell through to plain code.

- utils/mermaid.ts: accept any known Mermaid type as a diagram fence
  (gantt, timeline, flowchart, mindmap, sequenceDiagram, ...) and prepend the
  type keyword when the body omits it.
- Study panel + note preview both use it, so calendars/timelines render as
  SVG in chat and in saved notes. Ordinary code blocks are untouched.
- Tutor prompt now shows the exact expected fence shape.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
